{"title":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist Roadmap","role":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist","summary":"A Nuclear Medicine Technologist supports diagnostic and therapeutic procedures that use small amounts of radioactive materials (radiopharmaceuticals) to evaluate organ function, detect disease and, in selected settings, deliver targeted therapy.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Nuclear Medicine Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Nuclear Medicine Technologist supports diagnostic and therapeutic procedures that use small amounts of radioactive materials (radiopharmaceuticals) to evaluate organ function, detect disease and, in selected settings, deliver targeted therapy."},{"type":"p","text":"The professional works as part of a multidisciplinary team involving nuclear medicine physicians, medical physicists, radiopharmacists, radiologists, nurses and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Preparing patients for nuclear medicine procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Preparing and handling radiopharmaceuticals according to authorized protocols"},{"type":"h","text":"Operating nuclear medicine imaging equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Acquiring diagnostic images"},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring image quality"},{"type":"h","text":"Following radiation-safety procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Maintaining patient and procedure records"},{"type":"h","text":"Performing equipment quality-control activities within scope"},{"type":"h","text":"Supporting PET and SPECT workflows"},{"type":"h","text":"Assisting with nuclear medicine therapies under authorized supervision"},{"type":"p","text":"This is a radiation-sensitive clinical profession. Exact qualification, registration, radiation-worker authorization and scope of practice vary by jurisdiction and institution. In India, students should verify the applicable requirements of the relevant regulatory and healthcare authorities before employment."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Focus","Key Capabilities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Medical foundations"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, radiation basics"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine fundamentals"},{"text":"Radiopharmaceuticals, imaging equipment"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Clinical nuclear medicine"},{"text":"PET, SPECT, image acquisition"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Advanced practice"},{"text":"Quality control, therapy support, radiation safety"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist Trainee"},{"text":"Imaging and patient support"}],[{"text":"2–4 Years"},{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist"},{"text":"Independent technical responsibilities within scope"}],[{"text":"4–7 Years"},{"text":"Senior Technologist"},{"text":"Advanced procedures and supervision"}],[{"text":"7+ Years"},{"text":"Nuclear Medicine Technical Lead"},{"text":"Departmental technical leadership"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year-Wise Learning Plan"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical & Radiation Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"h","text":"Human anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Human physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Biochemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Pathology"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical terminology"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic pharmacology"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation biology"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare ethics"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient safety"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear medicine introduction"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Radioactivity"},{"type":"h","text":"Radioactive decay"},{"type":"h","text":"Half-life"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation units"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation detection"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation pr