Radiopharmaceutical knowledge"}],[{"text":"Medical Device Companies"},{"text":"Imaging equipment"}],[{"text":"Medical Physics Departments"},{"text":"Radiation safety + QC"}],[{"text":"Theranostics Centres"},{"text":"Nuclear imaging + therapy workflow"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Certifications & Professional Learning"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"PET/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"SPECT/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiopharmaceutical Handling"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Assurance"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Cardiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Image Processing"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Data Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"For clinical nuclear-medicine practice, recognized formal qualifications, radiation-worker requirements and institutional authorization are more important than generic online certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Nuclear Medicine Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Nuclear Medicine programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Medical Imaging Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Radiological / Imaging Sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Medical Physics"},{"type":"p","text":"Eligibility for medical-physics pathways can require specific undergraduate physics coursework."},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare & Research"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Clinical Research"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Biomedical Sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"MPH"},{"type":"h","text":"MSc Health Informatics"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. PET/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Whole-body PET"},{"type":"h","text":"Image quality"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"2. SPECT/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialize in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Functional imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Hybrid imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"Image-quality optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Nuclear Cardiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Work with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Myocardial perfusion imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiac function studies"},{"type":"h","text":"Stress imaging workflows"},{"type":"h","text":"4. Nuclear Oncology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Tumour imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Staging"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment response"},{"type":"h","text":"Theranostics"},{"type":"h","text":"5. Nuclear Medicine Therapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop experience in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Radioiodine therapy"},{"type":"h","text":"Targeted radionuclide therapies"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient preparation and radiation-safety procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"6. Nuclear Medicine Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Work on:"},{"type":"h","text":"New radiotracers"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging protocols"},{"type":"h","text":"Image reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"Theranostics"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-based image analysis"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist Trainee"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Nuclear Medicine Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized PET/SPECT Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technical Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical Lead / Supervisor"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Associate"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Imaging Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Device Route"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Application Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Application Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Imaging Product Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Technology Manager"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"h","text":"Theranostics"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the major growth areas in nuclear medicine combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Target identification","diagnostic imaging","targeted radionuclide therapy"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This is expanding the role of nuclear medicine beyond diagnostic imaging."},{"type":"h","text":"AI in Nuclear Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"AI can assist with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Image reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"Noise reduction"},{"type":"h","text":"Lesion detection"},{"type":"h","text":"Segmentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Quantification"},{"type":"h","text":"Image-quality assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Total-Body PET"},{"type":"p","text":"Extended-field PET systems can provide broader and potentially faster imaging, creating new opportunities in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Dynamic imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Whole-body tracer kinetics"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Personalized imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Image Processing"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern nuclear medicine increasingly uses:"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"Quantitative imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Automated segmentation"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-assisted analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Future-Ready Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy & Physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Nuclear Medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiopharmaceuticals"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"PET/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"SPECT/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Quality"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Safety"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment QC"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging Data"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"AI / Image Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"A particularly strong 2026+ positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Nuclear Medicine","PET/CT","SPECT/CT","Radiation Safety","AI Medical Imaging","Theranostics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Suggested Development Plan"},{"type":"table","header":["Period","Primary Objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anatomy + radiation fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Nuclear medicine equipment + radiopharmaceuticals"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"PET/SPECT clinical imaging"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Hybrid imaging + therapy + QA"}],[{"text":"Internship"},{"text":"Gain supervised nuclear medicine experience"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Build PET/SPECT technical expertise"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Specialize in oncology, cardiology or theranostics"}],[{"text":"5+ Years"},{"text":"Move toward technical leadership, research or clinical applications"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally be able to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Explain nuclear medicine principles"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand radioactive decay and radiation physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand radiopharmaceutical concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Prepare patients for nuclear medicine procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand safe radiopharmaceutical handling"},{"type":"h","text":"Operate or assist with nuclear medicine imaging systems under appropriate authorization"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand PET and SPECT workflows"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand PET/CT and SPECT/CT"},{"type":"h","text":"Position patients accurately"},{"type":"h","text":"Acquire technically appropriate images"},{"type":"h","text":"Identify common imaging artifacts"},{"type":"h","text":"Perform or understand equipment QC procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Follow radiation-protection principles"},{"type":"h","text":"Maintain accurate patient and procedure documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Communicate effectively with patients"},{"type":"h","text":"Work with nuclear medicine physicians and medical physicists"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand nuclear medicine therapy workflows"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand emerging theranostics"},{"type":"h","text":"Apply basic data-analysis skills"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand AI-assisted nuclear imaging developments"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Nuclear Medicine Technology","PET/CT","SPECT/CT","Radiation Safety","Image Quality","Theranostics"],"sep":"+","label":"Best positioning"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination provides a strong foundation for Nuclear Medicine Technologist roles and specialized pathways in PET/CT, SPECT/CT, nuclear oncology, nuclear cardiology and radionuclide therapy, while creating longer-term opportunities in research, medical-device clinical applications and AI-assisted nuclear imaging."}]}]}